omatin structure promotes binding of guanine-nucleotide releasing factor RCC1 to minor and major satellite repeats (By similarity). Chromatin-bound RCC1 maintains high levels of GTP-bound RAN near the centromeric heterochromatin, facilitating RAN-mediated microtubule nucleation during mitosis (By similarity). Plays a role in craniofacial development (By similarity). Required to maintain normal cell function in embryonic development (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}